# FLORA MCP in this repo

FLORA MCP (`search_docs`, `execute` at `https://agents.flora.ai/mcp`) is the **Cursor-side** FLORA console. Field Kit is the **product** console.

| Surface | Job | Auth |
|---------|-----|------|
| Technique Builder | Customize / publish heroes | FLORA app |
| FLORA MCP | List, retrieve schemas, optional ad-hoc runs | OAuth in Cursor |
| Field Kit `app/api/flora/*` | Recruiter demo + live programmatic runs | `FLORA_API_KEY` in `.env.local` |

## Do

- Prefer MCP `execute` for `client.techniques.list` / `retrieve` / `workspaces.list` when wiring [`lib/techniques.ts`](lib/techniques.ts).
- Call `search_docs` first if SDK method shapes are unclear.
- Keep Field Kit runtime on `@flora-ai/flora` in [`lib/flora.ts`](lib/flora.ts) — never route the Next.js app through MCP.
- If `execute` returns `403 paid_plan_required`, stop retrying. Inventory from public Technique pages in [`lib/clone-bases.ts`](lib/clone-bases.ts) until the workspace has API access.

## Do not

- Put `FLORA_API_KEY` in chat, MCP config, commits, or screenshots.
- Call `client.techniques.runs.create` or `client.generations.create` unless the user explicitly asked (billed).
- Author canvases from Cursor as the application artifact — that stays in Technique Builder.
- Replace demo mode with MCP. Recruiters use the live demo with no key.

After Technique Builder publish: retrieve the three heroes, then set `slug`, `viewLink`, and `status: 'ready'` in `lib/techniques.ts`.
